commit f7824935fc160d4366ba09c4b8b62ae329ec67ca
Author: <user> <rbr@holzforst-consulting.ch>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 22:50:15 2026 +0100

    Fix review findings: summary lookup, redaction, path checks, CLI

    - TextCache matches summaries by their node id, not a file-name prefix,
      so a turn no longer shows one of its steps' texts; decorate() reads the
      folders once and replaces (or clears) a node's text instead of merging.
    - Extra redaction rules are always global, so every match is redacted.
    - Session ids must be a single path segment, checked in the server and
      the store.
    - Hooks reach the engine on the port in engine.json, not only the default.
    - `mode` reports an engine error instead of claiming success.
    - `resume` and `status` pick the most recently active session, like the UI.
    - /text clears its timeout; ?level must be an integer.
    - Remove dead code, a duplicate import and misplaced comments.

